<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Assiniboia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1835–1870</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of Assiniboia was the appointed governing body of the District of Assiniboia, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-colony">Red River Settlement</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manitoba">Manitoba</a>, from 1835 to 1870. Chosen by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a> and presided over by the governor of Assiniboia, it made laws, organised courts and levied customs duties. Its authority collapsed in 1869 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-riel">Louis Riel</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> set up a provisional government.</p></div>
